"created_at":"2025-03-04T04:52:37Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T10:52:18Z","closed_at":"2025-03-06T01:37:28Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.4.stable.official [4c311cbee]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6603) - AMD Ryzen 9 5900X 12-Core Processor (24 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nSimple issue here, may just be a miscommunication. The migration guide states that read_string_from_stdin()'s new parameter \"buffer_size\" is optional. Currently I am getting an error when trying to use it the old way. If it's intended to be required the documentation makes no mention of a recommended size or what the buffer size used to be.\n\nFunction should probably be updated to have \"buffer_size\" be an optional parameter, or docs/migration guide should make a suggestion on what size developers need to supply in order to maintain original functionality.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a Godot project in 4.4.\n- Try to call OS.read_string_from_stdin() with no parameters in some way.\n- Observe the error.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[Buffer Not Optional.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19064233/Buffer.Not.Optional.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"skyace65","id":6080368,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwODAzNjg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6080368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65","html_url":"https://github.com/skyace65","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/following{/other_user}","gists_url":